{
  "_comment": [
    "Browser-open gate (ADR-0070). A launcher opens a browser only when every veto allows it: development only, never with a truthy TINA4_NO_BROWSER, never with --no-browser, never under CI.",
    "decision_table: resolved mode + process env + .env + flags -> opens. mode_table: how tina4 serve resolves the mode. A runner feeds every row to its real gate with the environment set for real, no mocks.",
    "Values are compared after trimming surrounding whitespace, case-insensitively. Process environment is resolved before .env."
  ],
  "version": 1,
  "decided": "2026-09-24",
  "adr": "ADR-0070",
  "truthy": [
    "true",
    "1",
    "yes",
    "on"
  ],
  "ci_env_vars": [
    "CI",
    "CONTINUOUS_INTEGRATION",
    "GITHUB_ACTIONS",
    "GITLAB_CI",
    "BUILDKITE",
    "JENKINS_URL",
    "TF_BUILD",
    "TEAMCITY_VERSION"
  ],
  "ci_not_set_values": [
    "false",
    "0",
    "no",
    "off"
  ],
  "rules": {
    "development": "framework: resolved debug mode on (TINA4_DEBUG truthy, unset is off, or an explicit debug argument). tina4 serve: --production -> production; else --dev -> development; else tina4-js -> development; else TINA4_DEBUG truthy -> development; else production.",
    "no_browser_variable": "TINA4_NO_BROWSER in the truthy set vetoes",
    "no_browser_flag": "--no-browser (or a programmatic no_browser=true) vetoes; no_browser=false never forces a browser open",
    "ci": "Under CI when ANY variable in ci_env_vars is set to a value that, trimmed and lower-cased, is non-empty and not in ci_not_set_values (false, 0, no, off). Maintainer decision 2026-09-24. So CI=true, CI=1, CI=yes and CI=woodpecker are CI; unset, CI=, CI=' ', CI=false, CI=0, CI=no and CI=off are not (any case).",
    "tabs": "at most one tab, the app URL; the CLI sets TINA4_NO_BROWSER=true for any framework server it spawns; only a primary process opens"
  },
